  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nCurrent upper level pattern shows westerly flow behind a departed\nlow well off the the northeast. While strong winds have subsided,\nbreezy conditions will return today under westerly, downsloping \nflow. Gusts around 25-40 mph can be expected, dropping off in the\nevening. Take care to not cause a spark as dry and breezy\nconditions persist. Ensembles do depict some weak energy moving \nover MT giving portions of south- central MT about a 10% or less \nchance of precipitation. Given the dry downsloping pattern, little\nto no accumulations are expected. Into the weekend, ensembles \nthen show troughing moving in late Saturday, giving high \nconfidence for a cool and wet pattern change. Ensembles have come \ninto better agreement on the latest run on the precip amounts \nacross the region. Currently, for Saturday night through Monday \nnight, the NBM is giving around a 30-60% chance for at least a \nhalf an inch of liquid precipitation across the lower elevations \n(highest across southeast MT), a 60-70% chance for area foothills,\nand 60-80% chance for area mountains. Area mountains have about a\n60-80% chance for at least 8 inches of snow with Beartooth/Red \nLodge foothills at about a 50-60% chance for at least 4 inches. \nOne caveat to this emerging pattern is that with where the low is \nsetting up, there is the possibility a portion of the region may \nsee significantly less precipitation from being in a dry slot of \nthe low. This will make a tricky forecast as the position of the \nlow is bound to shift. Keep an eye on the forecast leading up to \nthis event. Additionally, weak instability and modest shear will \nmake way for some weak thunderstorms Saturday. Ensembles generally\nkeep an active pattern going through mid week.\n\nHigh temperatures will be in the 60s and 70s today and Saturday,\ncooling into the 50s and 40s Sunday and Monday. Morning lows will\nbe coolest Monday and Tuesday mornings with temps near freezing. \nTake care to protect temperature sensitive plants. Temperatures \nreturn to the 60s low 70s by mid week. TS",
